  "question": {
    "text": "Let the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac></math> intersect the plane <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>&nbsp;at the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>. Let the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi></math> be the foot of perpendicular from the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> is the area of triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math>. then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "180",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>1</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>&#955;</mi></math></p><p>Any point on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>It lies on plane&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math>, so</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Direction ratios of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"&#60;\" close=\"&#62;\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Direction ratios&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"&#60;\" close=\"&#62;\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>.</p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8869;</mo><mi>L</mi></math>, so</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0125_3bcf90a75fbe.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 224px;\" /></p><p>Now,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>&#160;</mo><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"/><mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Hence,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>R</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>&#215;</mo><mover><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mi>P</mi></mrow><mo>&#8594;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd><mtd><mover><mi>k</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd><mtd><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>2</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mover><mi>i</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mover><mi>j</mi><mo>^</mo></mover></math></p><p>Therefore,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#215;</mo><msqrt><mn>144</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>576</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>&#945;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>720</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>180</mn></math></p>"
  }
}